"""BM05B-SRSS-TB(LF)(SN) - JST SH 5-pin 1.00 mm top-entry SMD header. Bare part.

Datasheet: JST SH connector catalogue (eSH.pdf, URL in pcb.toml). Specifications (p1): 1.0 A
(AWG #28), 50 V AC/DC, -25 to +85 C including temperature rise, 20 mOhm contact resistance
initial; AWG #32 to #28 wire. Header table (p3): BM05B-SRSS-TB, A = 4.0 mm (pin 1 to pin 5),
B = 7.0 mm body width; top entry type drawing: 2.9 mm body depth, 4.25 mm high; tin-plated
contacts and reinforcement. Mates with the SHR-05V-S(-B) housing (p2, B = 6.0 / 8.0 mm), 6.3 mm
above the board when mated (p1 top entry assembly layout).

Footprint: the top-entry PC board layout of p1: five 0.6 mm wide contact pads on a 1.00 mm
pitch, two 1.2 x 1.8 mm reinforcement pads (MP) whose inner edges sit 0.7 mm beyond the centres
of the outer contacts, 4.2 mm from the far edge of the reinforcement pads to the far edge of the
contacts and 2.65 mm to their near edge (so 1.55 mm long contact pads). KiCad library footprint
JST_SH_BM05B-SRSS-TB_1x05-1MP_P1.00mm_Vertical with its STEP embedded; the body outline sits
0.2 mm inside the reinforcement pads' outer edge (p1 "(0.2)").

The reinforcement pads are tin-plated metal tabs with no contact function (p3 "Reinforcement");
MP exposes them so the board can tie them to a net (usually GND) or leave them unconnected.
"""

prefix = config(str, default="P", help="Reference designator prefix")

P1 = io(Net)
P2 = io(Net)
P3 = io(Net)
P4 = io(Net)
P5 = io(Net)
MP = io(Net)

Component(
    name="HEADER",
    prefix=prefix,
    symbol=Symbol(library="BM05B-SRSS-TB.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("JST_SH_BM05B-SRSS-TB_1x05-1MP_P1.00mm_Vertical.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="BM05B-SRSS-TB(LF)(SN)", manufacturer="JST"),
    pins={"1": P1, "2": P2, "3": P3, "4": P4, "5": P5, "MP": MP},
    type="connector",
)
